**Definition 9.1 (falsifiers for the finite models).** The local finite
models are rejected by any of the following: a future reservoir suffix
changes a selected earlier reader state; a stop immediately after IN
loses or prematurely writes its bit; length zero performs a payload IN;
the relative ordinal zero or first cut is shifted; an out-of-cover target
is accepted because its request itself advances time; a later cover
changes an existing package's frozen target; a receiver is readable
before its seal; or omitting service choices still suffices for the full
extended state. These are tests of the stated local claims, not substitutes
for their quantified proofs.

